{
  "format": "sfxgen/1",
  "name": "Toggle switch",
  "description": "A chunky metal bat-handle toggle switch on an aluminium control panel, flipped up with a thumb, heard from the pilot's seat. First the lever passes centre with a small dull plastic tick. Then the spring throws the contact home, a hard, dry, dense clack (a crowd of tiny steel resonances gone at once, with the contact bouncing once just after), not a ping. At the same moment the thin panel it is bolted to takes the blow and answers with a short, boxy, slightly tinny \"tok\" that makes it sound mounted in something. Dry and close, like an aircraft cockpit.",
